# Templ retag

Composition layers do not own raw HTML. See `.project/retag.md` and ADR 004.

**Hidden-input registry SoT:** `fastygo.config.mjs` → `retag.allow` (not comments alone).

## Zones

- `internal/kit/ui/**` — atoms; raw HTML OK; do not retag / do not hand-edit codegen.
- `internal/ui/layout/**` — only `html|head|body|meta|title|link|script|noscript|main`.
- `internal/ui/{blocks,components,widgets}/**`, `internal/views/**` — **0 raw**, except allowlist.

## Allowlist (composition)

- `<input type="hidden">` — file must be listed in `fastygo.config.mjs` `retag.allow`; keep `// retag:allow: hidden input — …` above for readers.
- Any other raw tag only with `// retag:allow: <reason>` on the previous line (prefer kit extension).

## Prefer

| Instead of | Use |
| --- | --- |
| `<div>` | `@box` / `@stack` / `@group` / `@grid` |
| `<p>` / `<span>` / `<h*>` | `@text` / `@inline` / `@title` |
| landmarks | `@block` with `Tag` |
| prose `<a>` | `@link.Link` |
| CTA `<a>` | `@button.Button` with `Href` |

## Do not

- Add raw layout/typography/controls in registry/views.
- Add a new hidden field without updating `fastygo.config.mjs`.
- Increase retag debt; run `bun run retag` before finishing.
- Enforce ui8px here — brand utilities are intentional until FastyGoUI promotion.
